  "body": "This change improves the Tormach PathPilot milling postprocessor.\r\n\r\n### What changed\r\n\r\n- Raised `workOffsetMax` to 500 in `assets/posts/tormach.cps`. The post formats offsets 10 through 500 as `G54.1 P<n>`. Offsets 1 through 6 remain `G54` through `G59`. Offsets 7 through 9 remain `G59.1` through `G59.3`.\r\n- Raised `MAX_BOUND` in `camcraft_post::post::work_offset` to 1000 so the engine accepts work offsets up to 500.\r\n- Declared `millSpindleReverse = true;` in `assets/posts/tormach.cps`. The spindle start emits `M4` when `PARAM MillSpindle` is `reverse`. The spindle direction resets to forward (`M3`) on subsequent operations.\r\n- Removed `Tormach PathPilot` from `M3_ONLY_POSTS` in `tool_gate.rs`.\r\n- Refuses unsupported left-hand rigid tapping (`G74`) by name per Tormach PathPilot post processor guidelines, advising thread milling instead. Right-hand tapping cycles continue to emit `G84`.\r\n- Implemented control and wear cutter compensation (`G41`, `G42`, `G40`) with the `D` word on linear moves in `assets/posts/tormach.cps`. The post restores `G17` prior to compensation engagement or cancellation and refuses non-XY arcs while compensation is active.\r\n- Added unit tests in `crates/post/tests/tormach_post.rs`.\r\n- Added decision record `docs/decisions/4228-tormach-g54-1-p-m4-g74.md`.\r\n\r\nReason for new top-level test file: isolates Tormach mill post verification into a dedicated binary as no existing tormach directory suite exists.\r\n\r\n### Readings\r\n\r\n- Tormach UM10587: 770MX Operator's Manual (Version 0626A), Chapter 10 (G-codes, canned cycles, M-codes).\r\n- Tormach PathPilot Post Processor Guidelines (knowledgebase.tormach.com) for unsupported G74 left-hand tapping.\r\n- Public LinuxCNC G-code Reference (linuxcnc.org/docs) for G54-G59.3, G54.1 P, G84, G41/G42/G40, and M3/M4.\r\n\r\n### Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/post/tests/tormach_post.rs`:\r\n  - `tormach_extended_work_offsets_emit_g54_1_p`: tests G54-G59, G59.1-G59.3, G54.1 P10, G54.1 P100, G54.1 P500, and refusal of 501.\r\n  - `tormach_reverse_mill_spindle_emits_m4`: tests M4 spindle start and M3 reset.\r\n  - `tormach_left_hand_tap_is_refused`: tests named refusal for unsupported G74 left-hand tap.\r\n  - `tormach_right_hand_programs_remain_unchanged`: tests unchanged M3 and G84 output for right-hand tap.\r\n  - `tormach_control_cutter_compensation_g41_g42_and_g40`: tests G41/G42 with D word and G40 cancel.\r\n- `crates/post/tests/comp_plane.rs`: tests G17 restoration before engagement/cancellation and refusal of non-XY arcs during active compensation on Tormach.\r\n- `crates/post/tests/comp.rs`: tests wear compensation note on Tormach and removes Tormach from refusal loop.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/wear_comp.rs`: tests wear compensation posting through Tormach.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/control_comp.rs`: tests control compensation posting through Tormach.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/cutter_hand.rs`: tests M3-only refusal with Doosan DNM.\r\n\r\n### What was not exercised\r\n\r\n- Physical CNC hardware execution on a physical Tormach machine tool.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Tormach mill post: support G54.1 P1-P500 work offsets, M4 reverse spindle, G41/G42 control and wear compensation, and refuse unsupported G74 tapping\r\n\r\nFixes #4228\r\n",
